fix(dsc): map the dynamic-config page dyld reads at the top of the cache

mapSplitCacheSystemWide() does not map only the 43 cache files.  It appends one
more entry with fd == -1: a single page at sharedRegionStart +
header.dynamicDataOffset holding struct dyld_cache_dynamic_data_header, and the
kernel slides it with everything else.  Once shared_region_check_np() succeeds,
dyld dereferences that page unconditionally, before it looks at any image:

    SyscallDelegate::hasExistingDyldCache()   dyldMain, first thing it does
    reuseExistingCache()                      SharedCacheRuntime

both do strncmp((char*)(base + header.dynamicDataOffset), magic, 16).

kebab_dsc_build_plan() only produced the mappings the cache files declare, so
its extent stopped 0x4000 short of sharedRegionSize: exactly that page.  In the
real cache dynamicDataOffset is 0xaade4000, dynamicDataMaxSize 0x4000 and
sharedRegionSize 0xaade8000, so the missing page sits at
0x180000000 + 0xaade4000 = 0x22ade4000, immediately after the last mapping of
.42.dyldlinkedit.  A read there takes a translation fault, vm_fault() returns
KERN_FAILURE for the sub-map entry, and dyld dies on its first cache access
instead of ever seeing the cache.

Add the page to the main cache's mapping list: read-only, VM_PROT_ZF so that
vm_shared_region_map_file() creates an anonymous zero-filled object instead of a
file mapping, and slid with every other mapping.  The contents stay zero, so
dyld reports "mapped cache does not contain dynamic config data" and continues;
the kernel cannot write dyld's fsId/fsObjId, and pretending to would be worse
than saying so.  On the real cache the page's extent now ends exactly at
sharedRegionStart + sharedRegionSize, 0xaade8000.

Also grow struct kebab_dsc_header to the 512 bytes the mapping table starts at
so dynamicDataOffset/dynamicDataMaxSize (496/504) can be read and asserted, and
add the lines that made the remaining failures invisible: the ENOMEM paths in
the plan builder and for the mapping table, and a post-failure probe of
shared_region_check_np() so a failed vm_shared_region_map_file() says whether
the kernel's own rollback left the region empty or half mapped.

The is_main check in kebab_dsc_validate_header() compared sharedRegionStart
with plan->region_start, which had just been copied out of that same field, so
it could never fire; with the default slide of 0 nothing else looked at the base
either.  Compare against SHARED_REGION_BASE_ARM64 instead: every mapping is
entered at sms_address - sr_base_address, and a cache that declares any other
base can only be placed by accident.

Verified on the host only: the added page's end equals sharedRegionSize, it
overlaps none of the 51 cache mappings, and it survives every accepted slide
(0x55210000 leaves 0x8000 of slack).  No hardware.
